---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const coreCompetencies = [
  {
    area: 'Distributed Systems & Architecture',
    skills: 'Event-driven systems, high-throughput stream processing, idempotency, consensus models, fault tolerance',
  },
  {
    area: 'Languages & Runtimes',
    skills: 'Go (concurrency, profiling, low allocation), PHP 8.x (Swoole, RoadRunner, fiber runtimes), TypeScript, Python',
  },
  {
    area: 'Databases & Storage',
    skills: 'ClickHouse, PostgreSQL, Redis, RabbitMQ, Kafka, ElasticSearch',
  },
  {
    area: 'Infrastructure & Observability',
    skills: 'Linux internals, Docker, eBPF, Prometheus, Grafana, OpenTelemetry, Cloudflare Workers',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Engineering philosophy, background, and technical competencies of Sercan Kara."
>
  <article class="max-w-none">
    <header class="mb-10 pb-6 border-b border-neutral-200/70 dark:border-neutral-800/70">
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-50 mb-3">
        About Sercan Kara
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 font-mono">
        Senior Backend Architect &bull; Systems Engineer &bull; Istanbul, Turkey
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Bio / Narrative -->
    <section class="prose prose-neutral dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-[1.02rem] leading-relaxed mb-12">
      <p>
        I am a Senior Backend Architect and Systems Engineer with extensive experience designing,
        scaling, and operating resilient backend platforms. My focus centers on high-throughput data
        pipelines, low-latency API gateways, and distributed cloud topologies that remain stable under
        intense load.
      </p>
      <p>
        Throughout my career, I have architected mission-critical platforms: from regulatory 5651-compliant
        log management engines handling tens of thousands of network events per second, to multi-tenant B2B
        ITSM solutions and carrier logistics aggregators operating across Europe and the Middle East.
      </p>
      <p>
        I believe that the best architectures are boringly reliable. I prioritize operational transparency,
        clear failure domain isolation, and mechanical sympathy over hype-driven complexity.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Engineering Philosophy -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-neutral-200/60 dark:border-neutral-800/60">
        Engineering Principles
      </h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-neutral-200/70 dark:border-neutral-800/70 bg-neutral-50/40 dark:bg-neutral-900/20">
          <h3 class="font-medium text-sm text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-1">
            Simplicity over Cleverness
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
            If a system cannot be fully reasoned about at 3 AM during an outage, the architecture has failed. Keep boundaries explicit and avoid hidden abstractions.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-neutral-200/70 dark:border-neutral-800/70 bg-neutral-50/40 dark:bg-neutral-900/20">
          <h3 class="font-medium text-sm text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-1">
            Predictable Latency Profiles
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
            P99 and P99.9 matter far more than average latency. Understand allocation behavior, queue lengths, and GC pauses to prevent tail latency degradation.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-neutral-200/70 dark:border-neutral-800/70 bg-neutral-50/40 dark:bg-neutral-900/20">
          <h3 class="font-medium text-sm text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-1">
            Zero-Trust Resiliency
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
            Networks will partition, third-party APIs will fail, and disks will saturate. Every integration must have timeouts, retries with jitter, and circuit breakers.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-neutral-200/70 dark:border-neutral-800/70 bg-neutral-50/40 dark:bg-neutral-900/20">
          <h3 class="font-medium text-sm text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-1">
            Data Integrity as Core
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
            Write paths must be atomic and verifiable. In high-velocity pipelines, tamper-evident signing and immutable audit trails are non-negotiable.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Technical Competencies -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-neutral-200/60 dark:border-neutral-800/60">
        Technical Stack & Focus
      </h2>
      <div class="divide-y divide-neutral-100 dark:divide-neutral-800/60">
        {
          coreCompetencies.map((c) => (
            <div class="py-3 sm:py-3.5 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline justify-between gap-1 sm:gap-6">
              <span class="text-sm font-medium text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 sm:w-1/3 shrink-0">
                {c.area}
              </span>
              <span class="text-xs font-mono text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 sm:w-2/3 leading-relaxed">
                {c.skills}
              </span>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Contact & Direct Channels -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-4 pb-2 border-b border-neutral-200/60 dark:border-neutral-800/60">
        Get in Touch
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-4">
        I am always interested in discussing distributed systems, database internals, and architectural advisory engagements.
      </p>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-xs font-mono">
        <a
          href="mailto:contact@sercankara.dev"
          class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 hover:border-neutral-400 dark:hover:border-neutral-600 transition-colors"
        >
          contact@sercankara.dev
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/sercankara"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 hover:border-neutral-400 dark:hover:border-neutral-600 transition-colors"
        >
          GitHub ↗
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://linkedin.com/in/sercankara"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800 hover:border-neutral-400 dark:hover:border-neutral-600 transition-colors"
        >
          LinkedIn ↗
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
